From c077e63ae44a7b23e25cd1fae1d8ad232c18abc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:35:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] BOOTSPEED-1: boot stopwatch + boot sampler (diagnostic prints
 only)

EastSun 20260929: F5 takes 1-2 minutes before the HMI is usable. 14 boots today: 62-134 s, 59-112 s of it before the
op-log START line, where the console prints no times. LoadMachineConfig now starts (wb_serve.exe only) a sampler thread:
once a second for W906_BOOTSAMPLE_SEC s (default 180, 0 = off) it suspends the main thread, copies its IP and frame
chain (GetThreadContext / ReadProcessMemory only while suspended), resumes it, then writes
<W906_OPLOG_DIR>\bootsample_*.txt and every 5 s a "[BOOT ...] cpu NN%" line. No machine file, card or IO is touched.
Remove once the boot is explained.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
